<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Radar&amp;nbsp;DataFlow Phased Array Simulation Example&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example&amp;nbsp;Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example proposes radar system simulation with DataFlow phased array antenna designs. The traditional 3-layer architecure is applied with one target and one monostatic radar.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;For phased array modeling, the&amp;nbsp;pointing angle defined beam weights are calculated&amp;nbsp;by the BeamformerWeights parts and transferred to DataFlow Tx and Rx beamforming channels. Then the Tx envelop signal is transported to the Air Interface parts. The PhasedArray Tx and Rx parts are applied to transform the signal from Tx channel number sizing to target number sizing, then back to Rx channel number&amp;nbsp;(in this example is equal to Tx channel number).&amp;nbsp;After the virtual PhasedArrayTx, EchoGenerator and PhasedArrayRx, the signal sizing is transformed back to Rx channel number and the Rx beamforming is performed. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The RF impairment modeling configurations are realized in the equation &quot;SystemLevel_RFImpair_Params&quot;. The global RF impairment modeling &quot;Switch&quot; is shown at the top, while the following parts gives the parameter settings for &quot;No RF Impairment&quot; and &quot;With RF Impairment&quot;. This is proposed to the user as a&amp;nbsp;template to setup his/her own system-level RF impairment schematic.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The Tx waveformed is designed as simplified LFM, and signal processing chain is realized by pulse compression and PD. The range-doppler matrix and PD result are presented. The filtering incurred delay compensations (Const + ChopVarOffset after pulse compression part) are bypassed, since without filters in dataflow design no additional delays are involved.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The SystemLevel_Parameters equation provides all system level parameters, including phased array design parameters. After all simulations are done, the Equation_ResultPlots equation helps the user to plot the RD map and PD result figures.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ff0000 size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Folders in this workspace:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;Coupling 8*8 Case&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Defines an optional Tx element-to-element coupling design&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;2.&amp;nbsp;Radar_PhasedArray_Link&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Defines the system level radar design by &quot;RadarSys_Main&quot; schematic.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;Contains intermediate signal plots in various connection points.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
